e-label-term\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#archaic\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">archaic</a><span class=\"ib-comma label-comma\">,</span>&#32;<a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#rare\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">rare</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span>\n</p>\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#intransitive\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">intransitive</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> To walk about; to <a href=\"/wiki/wander\" title=\"wander\">wander</a> <a href=\"/wiki/aimlessly\" title=\"aimlessly\">aimlessly</a>.\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1989</b></span>, François Rabelais, “An Epistle by Pantagruel's Limosin”, in <cite>The Complete Works of Doctor François Rabelais</cite>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"en\">While we, alas&#33; must still <b>obambulate</b>, Sequacious of the court and courtier's fate &#58; O most infaust who optates there to live&#33; An aulic life no solid joys can give.</span></div></dd></dl></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2018</b></span>, Hulta Gertrude, <cite>Operation Selector</cite>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"en\">Dreaming of success, wealth and luxury, Deetee <b>obambulated</b> around the set in a leisurely manner.</span></div></dd></dl></div></li></ul></li>\n<li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#transitive\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">transitive</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> To <a href=\"/wiki/walk\" title=\"walk\">walk</a> or go up to, so as or as if to meet.</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Related_terms\">Related terms</h4></div>\n<div class=\"list-switcher-wrapper\"><div class=\"list-switcher\" data-toggle-category=\"derived terms\"><div class=\"term-list columns-bg ul-column-count\" data-column-count=\"2\"><ul><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/amble#English\" title=\"amble\">amble</a></span></li><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/ambling#English\" title=\"ambling\">ambling</a></span></li><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/ambulate#English\" title=\"ambulate\">ambulate</a></span></li><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/deambulate#English\" title=\"deambulate\">deambulate</a></span></li><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a href=\"/wiki/obambulation#English\" title=\"obambulation\">obambulation</a></span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Latin\">Latin</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Verb_2\">Verb</h3></div>\n<p><span class=\"headword-line\"><strong class=\"Latn headword\" lang=\"la\">obambulāte</strong></span>\n</p>\n<ol><li><span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#second_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">second-person</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#plural_number\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">plural</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#present_tense\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">present</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#active_voice\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">active</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#imperative_mood\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">imperative</a> of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\"><a href=\"/wiki/obambulo#Latin\" title=\"obambulo\">obambulō</a></i></span></span></li></ol>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐a